    "description": "Memory management skill for capturing new, durable facts, direct answers, life events, and temporal markers from the current text chunk, utilizing strict turn-level preservation and cross-referencing validation to ensure no critical conversational context (especially initiating turns) is dropped.",
    "instruction_template": "Skill: Insert New Memory\nPurpose: Capture new, durable facts, answers, and events from the current text chunk with strict turn-level preservation to ensure absolutely no critical context is lost, particularly session-initiating messages and temporal events.\nWhen to use:\n- The text chunk contains direct answers to questions (e.g., locations, plans, preferences, business ventures).\n- The text introduces new entities, significant life events, actions, personal updates, or hobbies.\n- The text contains temporal markers associated with an event.\n- The text represents the first 1-3 turns of a session (initiating turns).\nHow to apply:\n1. TURN-LEVEL SCAN: Explicitly identify the first 1-3 messages of the session and any messages containing temporal expressions (e.g., 'yesterday', 'last month', 'next month') or new event declarations.\n2. CROSS-REFERENCE VALIDATION: Compare your planned memory items against the raw session transcript. Ensure zero message omission for the identified key turns. If a foundational message is brief, it MUST still be stored.\n3. STRICT INGESTION: Every single message containing a proper noun, location, direct answer, or personal update MUST be stored. Do not omit conversational turns just because they are brief or seem trivial.\n4. AGGREGATION SUPPORT: Always include explicit, normalized temporal context (e.g., 'On November 22, ...') in the memory item to enable accurate time-bounded retrieval.\n5. DEDUPLICATE: Compare against retrieved memories to avoid duplicates. Split distinct facts into separate items.\nConstraints:\n- Do NOT drop information regarding personal updates, trips, classes, work changes, travel plans, or initial session greetings that contain facts.\n- Only skip purely conversational filler (e.g., 'Hi', 'How are you') that contains absolutely zero factual information.\n- Do not update or delete existing memories.\nAction type: INSERT only.\n\nOutput Format:\nACTION: INSERT\nMEMORY_ITEM: <content to store>\nREASONING: <why this action, including validation confirmation>",
