    "description": "Specialized skill for extracting and storing high-precision atomic facts (dates, locations, names, events) as standalone items to prevent data loss caused by lossy narrative compression or summarization.",
    "instruction_template": "Skill: Insert Atomic Fact\nPurpose: Extract and store critical, atomic facts as standalone memory items to ensure they survive storage compression without loss. This skill addresses failures where exact details (dates, locations, events) are dropped during summarization.\nWhen to use:\n- The text contains specific dates, times, or temporal markers associated with events.\n- The text mentions locations, addresses, or places.\n- The text includes names of people, organizations, products, or business ventures.\n- The text announces specific events, plans, milestones, or direct answers.\n- The text contains brief utterances that hold precise factual value.\nHow to apply:\n1. SCAN: Identify all atomic facts in the text chunk. Focus on entities and values that answer 'who', 'what', 'where', 'when'.\n2. EXTRACT: Isolate each fact. Do not summarize or paraphrase critical values (e.g., keep 'Woodhaven' not 'a town'; keep 'Nov 22' not 'soon').\n3. CONTEXTUALIZE: Formulate each fact as a complete, standalone sentence including necessary context. Example: 'User announced a hoodie line business venture on November 22.'\n4. SPLIT: If multiple distinct facts exist, split them into separate items. Never merge distinct facts into a single compressed summary.\n5. VALIDATE: Ensure no critical detail from the source utterance is omitted. Brief messages with facts must be stored.\n6. DEDUPLICATE: Compare against retrieved memories. Only insert if the fact is new or adds missing precision.\nConstraints:\n- Do NOT compress multiple facts into one narrative summary.\n- Do NOT drop information due to brevity of the source text.\n- Prioritize factual precision and retention over conciseness.\n- Only output INSERT actions.\nAction type: INSERT only.\n\nOutput Format:\nACTION: INSERT\nMEMORY_ITEM: <atomic fact content>\nREASONING: <extraction logic and fact type>",
