    "description": "Specialized ingestion skill implementing a self-verification gate and recency-based fidelity policy to prevent lossy summarization from dropping QA-critical facts like dates, locations, and specific events.",
    "instruction_template": "Skill: Insert Verified Detail\nPurpose: Ingest new memories with a mandatory self-verification gate and recency-based fidelity policy to prevent lossy summarization from dropping QA-critical facts (dates, locations, specific events).\nWhen to use:\n- The text chunk contains factual details that are highly likely to be queried (times, places, names, specific plans).\n- The conversation is recent or active, requiring high-fidelity retention.\nHow to apply:\n1. EXTRACT: Identify all critical factual details in the source text. Focus on temporal markers, locations, named entities, and key events.\n2. APPLY RECENCY POLICY: If the source text is from a recent or active session, DO NOT aggressively compress or summarize. Store the exact phrasing or minimally filtered dialogue turns to guarantee immediate answerability.\n3. SELF-VERIFICATION GATE: Before outputting the action, run an internal QA check. Ask yourself: \"If a user asks about this fact later, does this memory item contain the exact answer, or did I drop it as filler?\" If any critical detail is missing or over-summarized, revert to a higher-fidelity version that preserves the raw fact.\n4. CONTEXTUALIZE: Ensure the memory item is a complete, standalone sentence with normalized temporal context if applicable.\n5. DEDUPLICATE: Compare against retrieved memories. Only insert if the fact is new or restores missing precision.\nConstraints:\n- Prioritize factual retention and answerability over brevity.\n- Never drop specific dates, locations, or event details during compression.\n- Only output INSERT actions.\nAction type: INSERT only.\n\nOutput Format:\nACTION: INSERT\nMEMORY_ITEM: <verified, high-fidelity content to store>\nREASONING: <verification result and why this action>",
